# esbuild output generated at test-run time by phase1/gate3-layout-parity.spec.ts
# (gitignored, but Prettier doesn't read .gitignore). Kept in sync with the
# matching `ignores` entry in eslint.config.mjs.
phase1/fixtures/*.js

# The Phase 0 reference corpus is INPUT to byte-exact assertions, not prose to
# be tidied. `pnpm format` (prettier --write .) really did silently rewrite
# every *emphasis* to _emphasis_ in here, which changes the exact character
# offsets gate1-source-offset.spec.ts asserts its source-offset mapping
# against, and the exact rendered text gate4-export.spec.ts sweeps for an
# exact on-screen/PDF match. phase1/gate1-schema-fidelity.test.ts and
# phase1/gate3-layout-parity.spec.ts read the same files, so this one entry
# protects both suites. Deliberately the WHOLE directory rather than *.md:
# everything in it exists to be fed to a gate verbatim, including any future
# fixture that isn't Markdown. corpus/generate-long.ts is swept up by that and
# so no longer auto-formatted -- accepted, since ESLint still lints it (see
# below for why there is no matching eslint.config.mjs entry here).
phase0/corpus

# Committed gate result baselines, written by the gates themselves. Prettier
# stripped the no-newline-at-EOF markers off these, which shows up as spurious
# diff churn on every run and makes a real, meaningful baseline change harder
# to spot. Also a genuine .pdf/.png output directory, which prettier leaves
# alone anyway.
phase0/results

# NOTE on the "kept in sync with eslint.config.mjs" convention above: it does
# NOT apply to these two entries. ESLint only has matching config for JS/TS, so
# it never visits the .md/.json files at issue -- and phase0/corpus does hold
# one real .ts file (generate-long.ts) that SHOULD stay linted. Adding these
# paths to eslint's `ignores` would lose that for no benefit.
